>
  <p>Some concrete is simply done. When cracks run the full width of a slab, sections have heaved or sunk, or the surface is crumbling wherever you look, patching is money spent delaying the inevitable. <a href="/">Concrete Toronto</a> removes old surfaces and installs fresh, new concrete for a clean, modern look, across Toronto and the GTA.</p>

  <p>Replacement is also the chance to fix what caused the failure. We regrade so water drains where it should, and we build a compacted base sized for the load. The new surface starts life on a better foundation than the old one ever had.</p>

  <h2>What's included in our concrete replacement service</h2>
  <p>Every replacement job is priced as a complete package in a written quote:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Break-out and haul-away</strong> of the old concrete or asphalt</li>
    <li><strong>Excavation and regrading</strong> for proper drainage</li>
    <li><strong>A compacted granular base</strong> built for freeze-thaw conditions</li>
    <li><strong>Forms, pour and finish</strong>, broom texture or smooth where you want it</li>
    <li><strong>Control joints</strong> placed to manage shrinkage</li>
    <li><strong>Barricading, cleanup</strong> and clear curing guidance</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Repair or replace: the honest test</h2>
  <p>We quote both when both are on the table. Isolated damage on sound concrete is a <a href="/services/concrete-repair/">repair</a>. Widespread failure is a replacement. The difference in price is real, so we show you the condition of your surface and let the evidence make the case.</p>

  <h2>Why homeowners choose us</h2>
  <p>15 years, hundreds of concrete jobs across Toronto and the surrounding area. We show up on schedule, keep the site tidy, and back the new work with a 2-year warranty and a satisfaction guarantee.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>2-year warranty on every pour</li>
    <li>Satisfaction guaranteed</li>
    <li>Free, no-obligation quotes</li>
  </ul>

  <p>We replace concrete across the GTA, from Toronto to <a href="/locations/oshawa/">Oshawa</a> and <a href="/locations/north-york/">North York</a>. See every area on our <a href="/locations/">service areas</a> page.</p>
